{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.rows\n     2\t  \"Version-3 row codec. Pure row construction, graph decoding and canonical\n     3\t   cell numbering; no machine attachment, dependency scanner or transport.\n     4\t   An abstract row is {:kind keyword :slots vector}. Structural references\n     5\t   contain abstract rows; values use [:lit d], [:row abstract-row], [:cell id].\n     6\t   A task's :cells row holds alternating source identities and :cell-body\n     7\t   rows. Install children are separate tasks with separate cell scopes.\n     8\t\n     9\t   The census is ordered numerically by n (draft §3, \\\"sorted by n\\\"), so\n    10\t   :yin.k/c-10 follows :yin.k/c-9; its keys must spell c-N with no leading\n    11\t   zero, else :slot-kind.\n    12\t\n    13\t   Default value markers are plain maps {:yin.k/row abstract-row} and\n    14\t   {:yin.k/cell keyword}. A guest map whose sole key is :yin.k/row or\n    15\t   :yin.k/cell collides with them and is not portable: on encode one whose\n    16\t   payload is not a well-formed marker, and on decode any [:lit] of that\n    17\t   shape, is refused :yin.k/non-portable.\"\n    18\t  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n    19\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n    20\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n    21\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame :as frame]))\n    22\t\n    23\t\n    24\t(def profile {:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1})\n    25\t\n    26\t\n    27\t(def pending-table\n    28\t  {:next [:C]\n    29\t   :put [[:ref :stream] :V :D]\n    30\t   :ffi [:C :D :D]\n    31\t   :ffi-request [:D :V [:ref :stream] [:ref :stream] :C :D]\n    32\t   :link-request [:D :S [:ref :stream] [:ref :stream] :C :D :D]\n    33\t   :link-response [:D :S [:ref :stream] [:ref :stream] :C]\n    34\t   :install [:S]})\n    35\t\n    36\t\n  