{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"agent_message","text":"Ten survivors have been independently re-applied and killed by their named tests so far, with restoration verified after every run. R29 is not equivalent: removing the gate’s cycle check prevents the later graph check from returning the required `:cyclic` refusal. I also found that general task decoding can bypass the new marker refusal; I’ll verify that with a focused probe after the mutation campaign finishes."}}
