{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'budget|resource|byte' docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md | tail -20; rg -n 'Dart|marker|OOM' collab/1791980000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase6a-r2.report.md\"","aggregated_output":"590:Under this rule two lifts of one state are byte-identical. Two lifts of\n595:private resource entry seeded at its carried position; every `[:cell C]`\n609:Jing supplies canonical bytes and the digest of each body; this document\n623:1. **Gate.** Decode the wire map's canonical bytes retaining numeric\n641:   canonical bytes domain; exactly one row has role `:root`; kind rules\n665:   bytes and under portable decoded equality; optional absence has its\n674:   resource refusal of §10.10 if the bound is exceeded).\n709:11. **Composition.** Protection, resource, primitive and grant inputs of\n713:    private resource entry per cell, the parked table, children first\n725:the two kinds this carrier adds to UCF §7.5.4's set: `:byte-string` and\n744:  succeeds** (adequate composition, resource and admission inputs; a\n751:  lift's §6 numbering undoes resource remapping. Outside that context\n760:  controlled composition identities (occurrence, origin, resource\n798:   key equality, metadata, resource and profile requirements, refusal\n820:    a bound on decoded bytes, rows, cells, traversal depth, refinement\n822:    operational limit on top. Exceeding a local budget produces a\n823:    structured resource or capability refusal before any attachment, in\n828:    composition decisions and must not alter canonical bytes.\n838:the byte-string and metadata restrictions of §4; binding the row digest to\n854:private resource table, module-store instancing, scheduler state, the\n6:Engineer: claude-opus-5-5 (fresh session; the round-1 author, codex gpt-6.1-sol, is out of credits). Worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6a`, branch `srvm-phase6a`, HEAD 4b0e735e. Nothing staged or committed. The clock tool's time (09:31:56 GMT) is earlier than the brief's Created-GMT marker (09:40); I used the clock and did not invent a later time.\n16:- **Dart was not run by me**; per the brief the orchestrator runs it. Finding 1's fix can only be confirmed on Dart.\n60:| F6a malformed marker-shaped map encoded as `[:lit]` | `rows-test/marker-shaped-guest-maps-are-not-portable` | KILLED, 2 failures |\n61:| F6b marker-shaped `[:lit]` decoded | `rows-test/marker-shaped-guest-maps-are-not-portable` | KILLED, 2 failures |\n66:Finding 1 has no JVM mutant: the defect exists only on ClojureDart.\n70:1. **Dart failure at rows_test.cljc:238 (test change).** The multi-key `assoc` on the slot vector is now `(-> slots (assoc 2 …) (assoc 11 …) (assoc 13 …) (assoc 16 …))`. I searched both test files: there is no other multi-key `assoc` on a vector or nil. The remaining multi-key assocs (frame_test `reference-machines`, `tail-bookkeeping…`, the new `resume` helper) are on maps. **Dart is unverified by me; the orchestrator runs it.**\n95:   - **Encode:** a map whose sole key is `:yin.k/row` must carry an abstract row (`{:kind keyword :slots vector}`). A map whose sole key is `:yin.k/cell` must carry a keyword. Anything else of that shape is refused as status `:yin.k/non-portable`, kind `:marker`.\n97:   - My reading of the ruling: a guest map that *is* a well-formed marker cannot be told apart from a marker, so the default codec reads it as one. Only the malformed or literal collisions are refusable. The orchestrator should confirm this reading.\n126:| Dart | not run by me (orchestrator lane) | — | — |\n140:- `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc`: docstring (findings 6 and 8); `census-key` and `census-order`, and the `clojure.edn` require removed (finding 2); `structural?` takes kind (finding 2); gate installs check (finding 3); `marker-shaped?`, `value-node`, `decoded-value` (finding 6).\n147:  - new tests `unordered-containers-are-order-free`, `canonical-roots-are-pinned`, `census-is-numeric-from-ten-cells` and `marker-shaped-guest-maps-are-not-portable`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -I - <<'PY'\nimport runpy, pathlib, tempfile, subprocess, re, hashlib\nh=runpy.run_path('collab/6a-r2-mutants.py',run_name='review_import')\npaths=[pathlib.Path(h['FRAME']),pathlib.Path(h['ROWS'])]\norig={p:p.read_bytes() for p in paths}\nwith tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix='independent-6a-') as td:\n for p,b in orig.items():\n  q=pathlib.Path(td)/p.name;q.write_bytes(b);assert q.read_bytes()==p.read_bytes()\n for mid,path,needle,repl,ns,var,desc in h['MUTANTS'][:15]:\n  p=pathlib.Path(path);b=orig[p];s=b.decode();assert s.count(needle)==1\n  try:\n   p.write_bytes(s.replace(needle,repl).encode())\n   r=subprocess.run(['clojure','-M:test','-n',ns,'-v',ns+'/'+var],capture_output=True,text=True)\n   out=r.stdout+r.stderr\n   summary=re.search(r'Ran .*?tests containing.*?assertions\\\\.\\\\s*\\\\d+ failures, \\\\d+ errors',out,re.S)\n   print(mid,ns+'/'+var,'exit',r.returncode,summary.group(0) if summary else out[-1000:],flush=True)\n   print('\\\\n'.join(x for x in out.splitlines() if x.startswith(('FAIL in','ERROR in'))),flush=True)\n  finally:\n   p.write_bytes((pathlib.Path(td)/p.name).read_bytes());assert p.read_bytes()==b\n   print(mid,'RESTORED SHA256',hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),flush=True)\n assert all(p.read_bytes()==b for p,b in orig.items())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"R06 yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test/rule-boundaries-refuse-their-tamper exit 1 Ran 1 tests containing 9 assertions.\n2 failures, 0 errors\nFAIL in (rule-boundaries-refuse-their-tamper) (frame_test.cljc:287)\nFAIL in (rule-boundaries-refuse-their-tamper) (frame_test.cljc:287)\nR06 RESTORED SHA256 cff4a9c53000737b1b4a5f78d44eb9a20bbd73b40a37f6d4c85812dd5ea3712e\nR07 yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test/rule-boundaries-refuse-their-tamper exit 1 Ran 1 tests containing 9 assertions.\n0 failures, 1 errors\nERROR in (rule-boundaries-refuse-their-tamper) (PersistentVecto